  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the highest-priority need is to establish a clean, minimal baseline that isolates the simplest design choices. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most parsimonious configuration in the space: it uses a standard linear dimensionality reduction, a single profile, and no aggregation or fusion machinery. This gives a clear performance floor and a reference point against which every subsequent design decision (multiprofile, learned encoders like scvi/scgpt, image modality, aggregation strategy, fusion strategy) can be meaningfully compared. Running this first reduces uncertainty about whether basic RNA profiling is informative at all, and if it performs reasonably, it justifies investing subsequent experiments in adding complexity; if it performs poorly, it signals that encoder choice or modality matters more than profile structure. Under a limited budget, establishing this unambiguous baseline before layering on confounding factors is the most information-efficient use of the first experiment."
}

